-- title:
--   Avg Over Distinct Eligible Mass Eq Global Add Nonglobal
-- statement:
--   **Distinct eligible mass splits exactly into global mass and nonglobal mass.** For the given field-model parameters, strategy, family, and natural number $k$, let $E_k$ be distinct eligible mass, $G_k$ the globally consistent restricted mass, and $N_k$ the distinct nonglobal mass. Then
--
--   $$
--   E_k=G_k+N_k.
--   $$
--
--   The restriction defining $G_k$ uses global consistency of the tuple, so the equality separates precisely the globally consistent contribution from the remaining eligible mass.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.avgOver_distinct_eligibleMass_eq_global_add_nonglobal`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
